From 9a0bdc17a9f69884fb52c37b4fc4ca5e6e071c92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devilAPI <felixseiboldt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:56:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] axon7: GPS HAL from msm8996-common lineage-22.2, drop
 packages gone in 22.2

The 18.1 gps/ had no gnss@2.0 service, batching or geofence sources, so
android.hardware.gnss@2.0-impl/service-qti, libbatching and libgeofencing
did not exist. Take msm8996-common's 22.2 gps/ sources (same SoC and LOC
API); the device's gps/etc configs stay.

Drop PRODUCT_PACKAGES that 22.2 no longer has (kati: non-existent modules):
Snap (Aperture comes with LineageOS), the CNE client packages
(cneapiclient, com.quicinc.cne, services-ext), libqsap_sdk and
libQWiFiSoftApCfg (softap via hostapd), libicuuc.vendor and the duplicate
libstdc++.vendor (libstdc++_vendor stays). msm8996-common lists none of
them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i1nM3y1ifpqjS4n7PW
Change-Id: I07b3519a5999b080ed15debb78c07e7a874bfb7e
